{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1152965-would-you-guys-want-to-be-a-sin-eater","id":1152965,"title":"Would you guys want to be a sin-eater?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-25T16:03:02-07:00","id":1152965,"title":"Would you guys want to be a sin-eater?","content":"Let's say you die and was offer a chance to become one? Can you live a &quot;normal&quot; life with cool supernatural powers?<br /> <br /> Sin-eaters still age right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T16:18:39-07:00","id":1152972,"title":"","content":"I think they have an extended lifespan. So they age but slower.<br /> <br /> To be fair the drawbacks, at least in first edition, are more scant than other game lines. It is a true life, but you have the geist chattering at you and bugging you to do things, which probably wouldn't be good for people who want any sort of solitude.<br /> <br /> A lot would depend on the geist. If you're going to be living with someone for a hundred years you better hope you get along with them. This would be the big decider for me.<br /> <br /> Also the circumstances. If you were betrayed and killed by someone who is then going to kill others, vengeance is possible if you take up the Bargain, as would potentially saving lives. You might just believe you deserved more time, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-25-2017, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T16:22:55-07:00","id":1152974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1152965-would-you-guys-want-to-be-a-sin-eater#post1152965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's say you die and was offer a chance to become one? Can you live a &quot;normal&quot; life with cool supernatural powers?<br /> <br /> Sin-eaters still age right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends who is offering.<br /> &quot;Jill the overeater&quot; is different from &quot;Mary the Serial Killer.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/8fsIR2T.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13566-kalzky","name":"Kalzky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13566_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T16:56:55-07:00","id":1152980,"title":"","content":"No <span style=\"color:white\">10 characters</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T16:59:24-07:00","id":1152981,"title":"","content":"Yes (but I reserve the right to review my answer once 2nd edition is published).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T17:36:02-07:00","id":1152985,"title":"","content":"Sharing my brain with something else? No thanks, maybe next life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T17:58:04-07:00","id":1152990,"title":"","content":"Yes. If I'm dying before I think it's my time, of course I want another go around. I don't do loneliness, so company probably isn't gonna be an issue, unless Jimmy the Child Murdering Clown is shacked up with me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19270-princevertigo","name":"PrinceVertigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19270_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T20:47:38-07:00","id":1153032,"title":"","content":"Probably? I've got shit to do and my humanity is infectious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T08:10:09-07:00","id":1153176,"title":"","content":"Probably. I'm with Arc, I got shit to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T08:37:26-07:00","id":1153181,"title":"","content":"well, the other option is to die- so I'll take my chances with living with a mad voice of a crazy dead person in my head than not actually being alive at all. I'll also say yes for a Chthonian, Kerberos, a vampire offering the Embrace and almost any other vector of staying an intelligent being with all of the important body parts and that it would not require me to murder other people to stay alive (well, maybe except the Jackal mini template I wrote. Maybe. I hope I won't, but who knows what one would do in such situation?).<br /> <br /> In sort, sure, being alive as a supernatural creature has its disadvantages- but it is hell better than the alternative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T02:29:48-07:00","id":1153431,"title":"","content":"What are the pros and cons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T04:39:49-07:00","id":1153436,"title":"","content":"I mean, I would probably take the bargain and bind my self to a geist, unless the geist comes across as really unhinged or something, and it depends my mental state when i died (and why i died), but as i am now, I want to keep living, and cool powers and a buddy in my head sounds good.<br /> <br /> <br /> (also like shouldn't this be in the sin eater forum)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T17:54:42-07:00","id":1153843,"title":"","content":"Surely yes. The alternative is death, existence is wonderful and I got so much to do and experience. Getting a roommate in the head seems a trivial price for an extra century or so of life and cool supernatural abilities that empower me to pursue my goals much more than puny mortality. IIRC sin-eater candidates often tend to attract geists with somewhat compatible personalities, so it is even quite possible my geist and me can see eye to eye w/o too much trouble. A constant voice in the head might get annoying for the individualist me, but I'm adaptable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T13:17:31-07:00","id":1153964,"title":"","content":"Almost certainly. Sin-Eaters don't really have it that badly all things considered. They get to chill with their geist, who admittedly could make this pretty cool or terrible depending on their personality, and get to help ghosts get over their own shit. So I've got a buddy to hang out and go on terrifying adventures with on top of getting magic powers. I'm probably simplifying this a great deal, I'm not <i>that</i> familiar with Geist after all, but assuming that's the gist of it I don't see much of a problem with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}